      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-o/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"d = (5i + 4j) + 6(i + 3j) = 11i + 22j [M1] [A1] d = (5i + 4j) −6(i + 3j) = −i −14j . [A1] Alternative coordinate method. Write 𝐷= (𝑎, 𝑏). The gradient of 𝐴𝐵is (4 −(−2))/(5 −3) = 3, so 𝑦−4 = 3(𝑥−5) = 3𝑥−15 and 𝑦= 3𝑥−11. Thus 𝐷= (𝑎, 3𝑎−11). Use its distance from 𝐵. √ √(3𝑎−11 −4)2 + (𝑎−5)2 = 6 10 (3𝑎−15)2 + (𝑎−5)2 = 360 9𝑎2 −90𝑎+ 225 + 𝑎2 −10𝑎+ 25 = 360 10𝑎2 −100𝑎+ 250 = 360, 𝑎2 −10𝑎+ 25 = 36 𝑎2 −10𝑎−11 = 0, (𝑎+ 1)(𝑎−11) = 0. For 𝑎= −1, 𝑏= 3(−1) −11 = −14. For 𝑎= 11, 𝑏= 3(11) −11 = 22. These give the same two position vectors.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
